]
# user A still 3 lines and user B 2 lines over the next minute: the request is only applied once the
# cancel period (1h here) has passed.

## run 2: same config, -compactor.delete-request-cancel-period=30s -compactor.compaction-interval=20s
$ ... --id 3f2b1c9e-6d7a-4e0b-9c1d-2a8f5e4b7c60 --yes
matching lines now: 3
delete: HTTP 400 deletes in the future are not allowed
# Bug in the first version: the end was rounded up to the next second. Fixed: the end is floored and
# never after now (unit test "the end is never in the future"). The re-run could not be done: Docker
# was switched off on the laptop at this point (not run locally: Docker off).

## unit tests (mocked fetch), after the fix
$ node --test scripts/gdpr/loki-delete.test.ts
✔ builds a selector plus a line filter on the id
✔ rejects ids that could inject LogQL or match too much
✔ rejects a selector that is not a single stream selector
✔ the default range is the 7-day retention window, in whole seconds
✔ the end is never in the future (Loki rejects it with 400)
✔ explicit dates are used and checked
✔ submitDelete POSTs query, start and end in seconds with the tenant header
✔ submitDelete reports the error Loki returns
✔ countMatches adds the lines of every stream, with the range in nanoseconds
✔ listDeletes returns the requests Loki knows about
ℹ tests 10
ℹ pass 10
ℹ fail 0

